From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 02:16:24 +0200
Subject: net: dsa: lantiq: name the counters in the buffer manager's counter
 RAM

The counter numbers appear as bare hexadecimal in the string table and
nowhere else, so a reader has to take on trust that 0x1F is the received
packet count and 0x0C the transmitted one. Give each counter a name and
use it in the table.

The names are needed on their own account: the standardised statistics
groups read the same counters from a second place, and two places
spelling a counter number differently is a defect waiting to happen.

No functional change - every entry expands to the number it held.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

